  "date": "2026-11-14",
  "id": "3364",
  "title": "Minimum Positive Sum Subarray ",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "link": "https://leetcode.com/problems/minimum-positive-sum-subarray/",
  "topics": [
    "Array",
    "Sliding Window",
    "Prefix Sum"
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "You are given an integer array nums and two integers l and r. Your task is to find the minimum sum of a subarray whose size is between l and r (inclusive) and whose sum is greater than 0."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Return the minimum sum of such a subarray. If no such subarray exists, return -1."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "A subarray is a contiguous non-empty sequence of elements within an array."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Example 1:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Input: nums = [3, -2, 1, 4], l = 2, r = 3"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Output: 1"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "The subarrays of length between l = 2 and r = 3 where the sum is greater than 0 are:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• [3, -2] with a sum of 1"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• [1, 4] with a sum of 5"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• [3, -2, 1] with a sum of 2"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• [-2, 1, 4] with a sum of 3"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Out of these, the subarray [3, -2] has a sum of 1, which is the smallest positive sum. Hence, the answer is 1."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Example 2:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Input: nums = [-2, 2, -3, 1], l = 2, r = 3"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Output: -1"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "There is no subarray of length between l and r that has a sum greater than 0. So, the answer is -1."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Example 3:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Input: nums = [1, 2, 3, 4], l = 2, r = 4"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Output: 3"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Explanation:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "The subarray [1, 2] has a length of 2 and the minimum sum greater than 0. So, the answer is 3."
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "Constraints:"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• 1 <= nums.length <= 100"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• 1 <= l <= r <= nums.length"
    },
    {
      "t": "text",
      "v": "• -1000 <= nums[i] <= 1000"
    }
  ]
}
